&lt;li&gt;Scripts ou automação básica para configuração de dispositivos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Remuneração&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salário base:&lt;/strong&gt; R$ 9.000 a R$ 13.000 por mês&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefícios:&lt;/strong&gt; vale-transporte, vale-refeição e plano de saúde&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI Robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. We are based in North San Jose, CA and require 5 days/week in-office collaboration. It’s time to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Data Operations Lead to join Figure’s Operations org and lead the team that stands up new human data operations sites around the world. Data is one of the largest and most strategic functions at Figure, and this role owns how we go from zero to a running site in a new market. You will lead the people who launch new geographies end to end, entity and facility, hiring and training, hardware and software, partnerships and community, solving zero-to-one problems and coordinating with engineering and product at every step.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day one, you will own Figure’s data operations expansion: the strategy for where we go next and the team that gets us there. You’ll stand up new sites against volume, quality, and velocity targets, build the playbook that makes each launch faster than the last, and partner across engineering, product, and ops to make it happen. Specific responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the global expansion team that stands up new data operations sites, owning launches from site selection through steady-state handoff to local operators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and launch in new geographies, managing entity setup, localization, facilities, partnerships, and community building to establish presence in target regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously improve the expansion playbook: the repeatable systems, SOPs, and tooling that make each new site launch faster and more reliable than the last&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with engineering, product, and ops to develop the new hardware, software, and operational systems each site needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the expansion dashboard, tracking volume, quality, and throughput across sites daily, identifying bottlenecks, and shipping operational fixes fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, negotiate, and manage relationships with local partners, agencies, and vendors to accelerate market entry and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the connective tissue between new sites and internal teams, surfacing hardware and software friction, translating field feedback into actionable product improvements, and advocating for your team’s needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and lead the people running launches, growing the team as expansion accelerates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-10 years in Operations roles at startups and/or global corporations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up new locations in international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across cultures or in international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with strong project management instincts, comfortable managing multiple sites, partners, and workstreams simultaneously and keeping all plates spinning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to 5 days/week in-office collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in AI/ML companies or understanding of data collection for machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Spanish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Arabic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing physical-world operations in addition to digital platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $100,000 and $160,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is headquartered in San Jose, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone to build and lead our field logistics &amp;amp; dispatch function from the ground up. You will design the system and infrastructure to move robots and equipment between HQ/warehouse, active data collection locations, and customer sites and hire and manage the team that runs it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with the commercial operations and data operations teams, and you will have real authority to make the call on how this function is structured, staffed, and run as the company scales. This role requires excellent leadership, problem solving, and communication skills.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the function: Design and stand up the processes, SOPs, and checklists for kitting, dispatch, delivery, and returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and lead a team: Recruit, hire, and manage the coordinators and dispatchers who will execute day-to-day logistics as volume grows. Set the bar for how the team operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the equipment lifecycle end to end: Requests, scheduling, delivery, tracking, returns, inspection, and damage logging across every active site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the real-time source of truth: Establish the systems and tracking that give the company accurate, live visibility into equipment location, quantity, and availability across all active sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the transportation fleet: Manage the internal vehicle fleet and build the strategy for supplemental transport (leasing, carriers, couriers) as needs scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbook for contingency response when things go wrong in the field, and lead the response when they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years in logistics, dispatch, fleet operations, or field equipment coordination, with a track record of building or scaling a function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hiring, managing, and developing a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of physical equipment through a full cycle - dispatch, delivery, recovery, return.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward building systems and process rather than working around their absence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills - comfortable coordinating across multiple teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with tracking systems, spreadsheets, and project management tools (e.g., Google Sheets, Jira, Confluence, inventory systems).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment; comfortable making decisions in real time without waiting for permission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
