&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is headquartered in San Jose, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly organized and motivated&lt;strong&gt; Recruiting Coordinator&lt;/strong&gt; to support our People team and help scale hiring across engineering, operations, and manufacturing. This role is ideal for a professional who is excited to build strong recruiting foundations, drive process excellence, and grow towards a long-term career in talent acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate complex interview schedules across engineering, operations, and manufacturing teams, ensuring a seamless and timely experience for candidates and interviewers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hourly and high-volume hiring pipelines by managing candidate flow, scheduling screens, tracking progress, and partnering closely with hiring managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with sourcing efforts by identifying qualified candidates, managing outbound outreach, and maintaining early-stage talent pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Figure’s intern and university recruiting programs, including scheduling, onboarding logistics, event coordination, and candidate communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate and up-to-date data in our Applicant Tracking System (Greenhouse), ensuring reporting accuracy, compliance, and process consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to continuous improvement of recruiting operations by building documentation, templates, and scalable workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help deliver an exceptional candidate experience through proactive communication, attention to detail, and strong follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
