&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior Engineering Technician&lt;/strong&gt; to build, integrate, troubleshoot, and maintain complex robotic systems and engineering test assets. This is a hands-on role for someone who can work independently, own hardware within their area, and partner with engineers to drive problems to resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, integrate, bring up, and maintain complex robotic systems, subsystems, and test equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independently troubleshoot electrical, mechanical, and system-level failures&lt;/strong&gt; using test equipment, logs, data, and engineering documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own assigned hardware and test assets, including &lt;strong&gt;configuration, upgrades, maintenance, uptime, and readiness&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute system and subsystem testing and clearly identify, document, and escalate failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering to reproduce failures, validate fixes, and drive issues to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve procedures, tooling, fixtures, and workflows to increase &lt;strong&gt;reliability, quality, safety, and efficiency&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation of hardware configuration, test results, repairs, and known issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and support other technicians on hardware, procedures, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience&lt;/strong&gt; building, testing, troubleshooting, or repairing complex electromechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong electrical, mechanical, and system-level troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with complex assembly, system bring-up, rework, and component replacement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with diagnostic equipment such as multimeters, oscilloscopes, power supplies, logic analyzers, and DAQ systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Linux environments, shell commands, and Python for system bring-up, troubleshooting, test execution, and data collection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read electrical schematics, wiring diagrams, mechanical drawings, CAD, BOMs, and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with robotics, automation, or complex electromechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system integration, reliability testing, or failure analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CATIA or similar CAD tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python, Java, and/or C++ experience.&lt;/li&gt;
