&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is based in San Jose, CA and requires 5 days/week in-office collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Gear Design Engineer to own gear and transmission design for our humanoid robot&#39;s hands — some of the most power-dense, space-constrained actuators in the world. You will take gear trains from first-principles sizing through validation and into mass manufacturing, defining how our robot grasps and manipulates the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own gear design end-to-end: system-level sizing, macro and micro geometry definition, rating and life analysis, prototyping, validation, and ramp to mass production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform gear sizing, contact/bending stress analysis, and micro-geometry optimization (profile and lead modifications) in KISSsoft to meet efficiency, durability, backlash, and NVH targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design gears, shafts, and transmission assemblies in 3D CAD (CATIA) that satisfy extreme packaging, load, and durability requirements of a high-DOF robotic hand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define gear manufacturing strategy — cutting, grinding, powder metal, MIM, or plastics — and drive DFM with suppliers from first articles through high-volume production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate accurate 2D drawings with gear data tables and GD&amp;amp;T per ASME Y14.5, and define inspection and metrology plans for incoming quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run test rigs to characterize efficiency, backlash, wear, and fatigue life; correlate test data back to analytical models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with actuator, structures, EE, and manufacturing teams — proactively identifying risks, driving decisions, and unblocking the program without waiting to be asked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience designing gears and geared transmissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, Mechatronics, or similar field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of complete gear designs from initial sizing through mass manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in KISSsoft (or equivalent) for gear rating, contact analysis, and micro-geometry optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CATIA (or equivalent high-end 3D CAD) for complex geometry and large assemblies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of AGMA/ISO gear rating standards, gear metrology, and tolerancing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with gear manufacturing processes (hobbing, shaping, skiving, grinding, powder metal, MIM, or injection molding) and supplier development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong team player with a high sense of agency — you take ownership of outcomes, communicate openly, and elevate the people around you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with small-module, high-ratio, or high-power-density gearing (planetary, cycloidal, or strain wave)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in robotics, surgical devices, aerospace actuation, or automotive e-drive transmissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with lubrication selection, grease DOE, and tribology for compact gearboxes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fatigue modeling, bearing life characterization, and accelerated life testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a product through NPI builds (EVT/DVT/PVT) and FATP at volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this&amp;nbsp;&lt;em class=&quot;chrome-extension-mutihighlight chrome-extension-mutihighlight-style-2&quot;&gt;full&lt;/em&gt;-time position is between $160,000 - $250,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is based in San Jose, CA and require 5 days/week in-office collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;We&#39;re seeking an experienced Logistics and Trade Compliance Analyst to manage end-to-end customs clearance and regulatory compliance for both inbound and outbound shipments. This role owns the accuracy and efficiency of our cross-border logistics operations, working closely with customs brokers, freight forwarders, carriers, and internal stakeholders (GSM, MPM, Production) to ensure timely clearance while minimizing compliance risk and duty exposure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate brings strong international logistics and trade compliance expertise, along with the ability to apply AI/data analytics tools to improve classification accuracy, flag anomalies, and streamline logistics operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;• Coordinate end-to-end international shipping operations across ocean, air, and ground freight, managing multiple carriers, freight forwarders, and 3PLs across regions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;• Manage logistics documentation (bills of lading, commercial invoices, packing lists, certificates of origin) to support smooth cross-border movement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;• Track shipments proactively across the supply chain, resolving delays, routing issues, or carrier exceptions before they impact delivery timelines&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot;&gt;• Coordinate with overseas suppliers, vendors, and regional logistics partners to align shipping schedules, Incoterms, and documentation requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot;&gt;• Optimize freight costs and transit times by evaluating carrier performance, routing options, and mode of transport (air vs. ocean vs. ground)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot;&gt;• Manage import customs clearance process, ensuring accurate HTS classification, valuation, and country-of-origin determinations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;• Review and audit customs entries filed by brokers for accuracy; resolve discrepancies with CBP or other customs authorities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;14&quot;&gt;• Track and reconcile tariff classifications against product changes/updates from engineering or procurement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot;&gt;• Manage export documentation, licensing determinations (ECCN/EAR, ITAR if applicable), and screening against denied party lists&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot;&gt;• Ensure compliance with export control regulations (BIS, OFAC, State Department where relevant)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;17&quot;&gt;• Coordinate with freight forwarders on export declarations (EEI/AES filings) and required certificates of origin&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;18&quot;&gt;• Manage compliance and logistics requirements for Dangerous Goods (specifically Lithium-Ion Batteries)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;19&quot;&gt;• Use AI-powered tools and data analytics platforms to support HTS classification accuracy, duty spend analysis, and trade data reconciliation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;20&quot;&gt;• Build or utilize dashboards/models to detect anomalies in customs entries, shipment delays, or compliance exceptions before they become issues&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;21&quot;&gt;• Apply predictive analytics to forecast duty costs, tariff exposure, and clearance timelines for supply chain planning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot;&gt;• Use data-driven insights to identify process inefficiencies and recommend automation opportunities across inbound/outbound workflows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;23&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;24&quot;&gt;• 5-7 years of proven experience in tracking, tracing, and managing international freight operations (ocean, air, ground) and working with global carriers, forwarders, and 3PLs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;25&quot;&gt;• Strong working knowledge of Customs clearance requirements in the USA, HTS classification, import/export regulations, section 301, and section 232&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26&quot;&gt;• Strong analytical skills; comfortable auditing entries, reconciling data, and identifying trends&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;• Excellent cross-functional communication—this role interfaces with internal and external stakeholders regularly, working across multiple time zones and cultures with overseas suppliers/partners&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;29&quot;&gt;• Bachelor&#39;s degree in supply chain, international business, or a related engineering/analytical field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;30&quot;&gt;• Hands-on experience applying AI/data analytics tools in a logistics and trade compliance context&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $120,000 - $175,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is based in San Jose, CA and requires 5 days/week in-office collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, hands-on execution role for someone who&#39;s comfortable operating at both altitudes, thinking through systems and processes at a high level, then rolling up their sleeves to get the day-to-day right. You&#39;ll own HR operations end to end, acting as the go-to person for our HR platforms and vendor relationships, keeping leaves and accommodations running smoothly, and staying on top of compliance for our hourly workforce. You have a knack for taking undefined, messy processes and turning them into systems that just work at scale, and you&#39;re always looking for ways to make the employee experience better at every stage of the journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Lifecycle &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the employee lifecycle end-to-end (onboarding, job changes, offboarding, records, verifications), ensuring every step is seamless, compliant, and audit ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously audit and elevate the employee experience, gathering feedback to remove operational friction and build a high empathy, high efficiency workplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted point of contact for employee HR inquiries, resolving tickets within SLAs and handling complex escalations with judgment and discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage statutory leaves end-to-end and lead interactive medical accommodation processes, coordinating state disability integration, communications, and return-to-work logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the compliance escalation point for garnishments, complex leave cases, and sensitive offboarding events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll, Benefits &amp;amp; Hourly Workforce&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run accurate, end-to-end payroll for exempt and non-exempt teams, including final pay calculations, severance, and leave-related adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strict timekeeping hygiene across hourly populations, tracking daily punch accuracy, shift differentials, and meal/rest break compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our benefits broker to manage health, 401(k), and wellness programs; lead annual Open Enrollment and evaluate benefit competitiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit and reconcile monthly carrier billings, benefit feeds, and agency staffing invoices to eliminate financial discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programs, Projects &amp;amp; Data Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as primary system administrator for our People tech stack (HRIS, timekeeping, ticketing), managing configurations, permissions, workflows, and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the broader People team on compensation and job architecture (levels, job families, pay bands), keeping system data clean and current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Partner to build and maintain a centralized People Ops knowledge repository (SOPs, handbooks, compliance calendars) to maximize self-service support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain uncompromising data integrity across headcount, worker classifications, shift assignments, and equity data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional People projects as we scale, from org design updates to vendor evaluations and policy rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of progressive People Operations experience in a high-growth tech, or robotics environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience configuring workflows, permissions, and integrations; direct experience administering Rippling is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience partnering with benefits brokers/platforms and leading annual Open Enrollment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success processing multi-state payroll, enforcing non-exempt timecard compliance, and supporting contingent/agency workforces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of California employment law, FLSA classifications, and benefits administration frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $110,000 – $200,000. The pay range for this role reflects the two levels at which it may be filled (Specialist or Senior Specialist). Final leveling, title, and placement within the range will be determined based on the candidate&#39;s relevant experience and skill set. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A Figure é uma empresa de robótica e IA que desenvolve robôs humanoides autônomos de uso geral. O objetivo da empresa é lançar robôs humanoides com inteligência de nível humano. Seus robôs são projetados para executar uma grande variedade de tarefas nos mercados residencial e comercial. A Figure tem sede em San Jose, Califórnia, e está estabelecendo sua primeira unidade de operações de dados no Brasil.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Estamos construindo a base de dados que dá vida aos nossos robôs humanoides. O time de Data Operations cria e faz a curadoria dos dados que treinam nossos sistemas de IA, e a organização de Data Creators é responsável por como esses dados são capturados, em que volume e com qual padrão de qualidade, em todas as nossas unidades.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Como &lt;strong&gt;Shift Coordinator (Coordenador de Turno)&lt;/strong&gt;, você conduz a operação de coleta do dia a dia no turno sob sua responsabilidade. Enquanto o seu turno está rodando, o chão de operação é seu: você sequencia o trabalho de captura entre os Data Creators e as estações, resolve problemas em tempo real e garante que o turno bata as metas de cobertura e de produção.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jornada:&lt;/strong&gt; Operação 24/7, com múltiplos turnos rotativos (Manhã, Tarde e Noite). Os horários estão listados abaixo. Alguma flexibilidade para rodízio de turnos pode ser necessária.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manhã (Day): das 6h às 15h&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tarde (Swing): das 14h30 às 23h30&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Noite (Night): das 23h às 8h&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsabilidades&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduzir a operação de coleta do dia a dia do seu turno, com foco nas metas de volume e qualidade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sequenciar e distribuir o trabalho de captura entre os Data Creators e as estações, ajustando em tempo real conforme as prioridades mudam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolver na hora problemas de hardware, captura, equipe e instalações; escalar bloqueios que ultrapassem o turno.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Garantir a cobertura do turno: gerenciar pausas, ausências e rodízio para que as estações de captura nunca fiquem descobertas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduzir passagens de turno estruturadas, documentando produção, pendências e status dos equipamentos para o turno seguinte.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Garantir a aderência aos SOPs (procedimentos operacionais padrão) e às diretrizes de segurança e ergonomia no chão de operação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atuar em parceria com os Project Coordinators e o time de Data Quality para identificar e resolver problemas no momento da criação dos dados.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reportar à liderança da unidade a produção do turno, o downtime (tempo parado) e os problemas recorrentes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requisitos&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2+ anos em operações, produção, logística ou supervisão de turno, com experiência conduzindo a execução do dia a dia de uma equipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiência coordenando pessoas e prioridades em tempo real, em um ambiente físico e dinâmico.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conforto para tomar decisões rápidas com informação incompleta e bom senso sobre quando escalar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comunicação clara; capacidade de fazer passagens de turno bem organizadas e manter registros de turno precisos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disponibilidade para trabalhar em turnos rotativos, incluindo noites e fins de semana (com adicional noturno).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inglês em nível profissional (SOPs, dashboards e escalações envolvem times nos EUA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Diferenciais&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiência com robótica, sistemas autônomos, captura de movimento (motion capture) ou dados para IA física.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiaridade com hardware de captura de movimento ou sensores vestíveis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiência em operações de startups em rápido crescimento.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiência prévia em operações 24/7 ou multiturno.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Remuneração&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salário base:&lt;/strong&gt; R$ 8.000 a R$ 13.000 por mês&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefícios:&lt;/strong&gt; vale-transporte, vale-refeição e plano de saúde&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

