&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively advocate for and influence strategic initiatives at the company level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with internal and external senior stakeholders at the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical grasp of security &amp;amp; privacy fundamentals, including enterprise controls, SDLC, machine learning, cryptography, data protection, network security, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating global privacy compliance programs (GDPR, CCPA, DSA, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating industry certification, such as SOC-2, NIST, ISO 27001, ISO/TR 22100-4, IEC/TR 63074&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors in a technical field such as Computer Science or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience leading teams and large scale programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $150,000 - $350,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is based in San Jose, CA and requires 5 days/week in-office collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technical Recruiter will be responsible for attracting top talent to tackle the complex challenges of developing general purpose humanoid robots, supporting high-volume hiring across a wide range of technical and operational functions with an initial focus on Commercial and Operations, and expanding to Mechanical, Manufacturing, Software, AI, Controls, Systems Integration &amp;amp; Test (SI&amp;amp;T), and beyond as needs evolve.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires the ability to manage a large, fast-moving pipeline across multiple concurrent functions, and to pivot quickly as hiring priorities shift from one team to the next. The ideal candidate will focus on scaling the team intentionally, ensuring that we not only grow headcount but also find the right individuals who align with our core values of moving quickly and maintaining a mission-driven focus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end recruitment across multiple concurrent requisitions spanning Commercial and other technical/operational functions (Mechanical, Manufacturing, Software, AI, Controls, SI&amp;amp;T, etc.), sourcing, screening, and interviewing candidates at volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a diverse and robust candidate pipeline through direct sourcing, networking, and leveraging recruitment platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers across multiple functions simultaneously to understand each team&#39;s specific needs and provide tailored, fast-adapting recruitment strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly ramp up on new functional areas as hiring priorities shift, applying strong foundational sourcing and screening skills across unfamiliar technical domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and leverage key recruiting metrics across all supported functions to continuously optimize the recruitment process and meet aggressive hiring goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a positive candidate experience throughout all stages, reflecting Figure&#39;s values and fostering long-term engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements to the technical interview process, ensuring timely communication and feedback between candidates and hiring teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support seamless onboarding for new hires, collaborating with People and technical teams to ensure a smooth transition into the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience recruiting for technical and/or operational roles, with demonstrated success managing high-volume pipelines across multiple functions simultaneously in fast-growing tech or manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to pivot quickly between different hiring functions and ramp up on new technical domains with minimal ramp time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in sourcing passive candidates and building a diverse talent pipeline through various methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with recruitment tools and platforms (e.g., Greenhouse, LinkedIn Recruiter) to manage a large, multi-function req load efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build relationships, provide strategic advice, and challenge hiring managers when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting across Commercial, Mechanical, Manufacturing, Software, AI, or Controls functions specifically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the technical landscape and the unique challenges in recruiting for AI, robotics, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting at a staffing or search agency, with exposure to managing multiple concurrent client requisitions across varied technical domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about fostering diversity and inclusion in the workplace, with a track record of promoting diverse hiring practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $120,000 - $200,000 annually.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended. Leveling and title may be adjusted based on candidate experience and feedback throughout the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a User Support Lead to build, run, and scale our user support team. Your team will be the first line of response for our users. Its core mission is to surface, reproduce, and route bugs in our internal application quickly and accurately so that engineering can fix what matters most. You will own the support operation end to end: the people, the processes, and the tooling. This is a high-ownership role where great support work directly improves the quality of the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full user support function: strategy, day-to-day operations, tooling, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate the support queue, ensuring inbound issues are answered, investigated, and resolved within response-time and satisfaction targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the team: hire, onboard, coach, and manage support specialists as volume and scope grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design workflows that turn user reports into well-documented, reproducible, prioritized bug tickets for engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, configure, and continuously improve our support stack using platforms such as Sierra and Intercom, including AI agent flows, macros, and escalation paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain internal documentation, triage playbooks, and a self-serve knowledge base to deflect repeat issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and report on key metrics for both support performance (CSAT, first response time, resolution time) and bug discovery (time to reproduction, escalation accuracy, defect signal quality)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the escalation point for complex, sensitive, or high-priority issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering and product to triage findings, identify recurring pain points, and close the loop with affected users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in user or customer support for a software product, including 2+ years building or leading a support team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience administering and optimizing modern support platforms such as Sierra, Intercom, or similar tools (e.g., Zendesk, Front, Ada)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience deploying and tuning AI-powered support agents, including flow design, guardrails, and escalation logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical troubleshooting instincts: able to reproduce issues, isolate variables, and write bug reports engineers can act on immediately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building a support operation from scratch or scaling one significantly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication: clear, warm, and precise with users and internal teams alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills; comfortable using support data to drive decisions and report to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running support for internal tools or technical user bases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with JIRA (or similar) for bug triage and cross-team escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with QA or defect management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining SLAs and building QA programs for support quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for helping scale the deployment of humanoid robots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $120,000 - $175,000 annually.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended. Leveling and title may be adjusted based on candidate experience and feedback throughout the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is headquartered in San Jose, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Warehouse Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to run our warehouse of robots, spare parts, and equipment supporting customer deployments and field data operations. This role owns everything that happens to equipment inside the four walls - receiving, storage, inspection, kitting, and inventory accuracy -&amp;nbsp; and hands off completed kits to the Dispatch team for delivery to the field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day operations of the warehouse: layout, storage, labeling, and organization of robots, spare parts, and data collection equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive incoming equipment and shipments; inspect, log condition, and check items into inventory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and stage kits against project request manifests, and hand off completed kits to the Dispatch Coordinator for delivery to active sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate, real-time inventory records - quantities, condition, and location - for all equipment held in the warehouse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect and process returned equipment, documenting damage or missing items and routing gear for repair, restock, or retirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage warehouse safety, cleanliness, and compliance, including proper storage and handling of batteries, tools, and sensitive equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, train, and manage warehouse staff or temp labor as volume grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Deployment Logistics Lead and Dispatch Coordinator to forecast equipment needs and flag shortages or bottlenecks before they impact a project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and maintain SOPs/checklists for receiving, kitting, inspection, and returns as the program scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track equipment lifecycle data (usage, wear, repair history) to support replacement and purchasing decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years experience in warehouse management, inventory control, or equipment operations, ideally in a hardware, robotics, or field-deployed equipment environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning physical inventory accuracy at scale - not just receiving, but full lifecycle tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and meticulous attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills - comfortable coordinating across logistics, dispatch, and project teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with inventory/tracking systems, spreadsheets, and project management tools (e.g., Google Sheets, Jira, Confluence, inventory systems).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or leading a small team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with physical work: lifting equipment, operating warehouse equipment (pallet jacks, forklifts, etc.) as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment; comfortable solving problems in real time without waiting for permission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in robotics, autonomous vehicles, or hardware company warehouse operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with inventory management systems or ERP tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forklift certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting rapid scaling of a field operations or deployment program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $150,000 - $200,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is headquartered in San Jose, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Electrical Hardware Engineer to support the design, development, and integration of wire harness and electrical interconnect systems for humanoid robotic platforms. This role will drive 2D and 3D wire harness design, routing, and integration within complex electromechanical assemblies, ensuring optimal performance, manufacturability, and reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is highly proficient in 3D CAD, detail-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced startup environment with close collaboration across EE, ME, and Manufacturing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain 3D wire harness routing within system-level assemblies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create 2D harness drawings, flatten layouts, and manufacturing documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define connector selection, backshells, strain reliefs, and mounting features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with EE to translate schematics into physical harness designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure proper bend radius, shielding, separation, and routing best practices in line with EWIS/USCAR standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support BOM creation and part selection for harness and connector components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with suppliers and contract manufacturers for DFM feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update models and drawings based on prototype learnings and MFG feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain revision control and proper documentation in PLM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in wire harness or electrical hardware design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in 3D CAD (e.g., CATIA, SolidWorks, Creo, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating both 2D and 3D harness documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of harness routing constraints and electrical integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with contract manufacturers and suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a startup environment with fast iteration cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with robotics or complex electromechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EVT/DVT build support experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PLM systems (e.g., Enovia)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting manufacturing floor issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $125,000 - $225,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
